\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri393\sl244\slmult1\sb1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 At the Main Screen, click on File, then Open (from all saved tests) to open the XCHVSTK.PTI test file from the Examples folder.\expnd13\expndtw63  \expnd0\expndtw0 Back at the Main Screen, click on Engine to open the Engine Specs menu.\expnd13\expndtw63  \expnd0\expndtw0 At the Engine Specs menu, click on File,\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 then\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Open\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Example\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Engine\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 to open\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 X350MLD.PTI\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 engine\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 file.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 The\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 program\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 displays\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Example\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Engine\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Library\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 provided with the program by Performance Trends.\expnd14\expndtw71  \expnd0\expndtw0 These files represent different engine/camshaft combinations which have been\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 created with the Port Flow Analyzer.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 You can also add other combos to a similar library called Saved Engines.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Click on X350MLD.PTI and then click on\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\sl-227\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Open \expnd0\expndtw-2 button.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb7\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri7792\sl244\slmult1\sb1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 The program will return you to the Engine Specs menu so you can see the specs for this file.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Also note\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 that the Current Engine is X350MLD.PTI at the top of this menu.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 While reviewing the Engine Specs data file for X350MLD.PTI, you see it is a 4.00 x 3.48 350 CID V-8 with 9.3 compression, and a very mild cam.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 (The MLD in X350MLD.PTI stands for mild cam.)\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Return\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 to\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd-1\expndtw-5  \expnd0\expndtw0 Main\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 Screen\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 by clicking on Back (ok) at the top left of the menu or pressing the <Exc> key.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 (This is very similar to what was done in Example 4.3 to make Engine Graphs.)\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri7951\sl244\slmult1\sb224\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 By opening the XCHVSTK.PTI Flow\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \expnd0\expndtw0 Test\expnd-2\expndtw-8  \expnd0\expndtw0 and\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \expnd0\expndtw0 X350MLD.PTI Engine Specs file, you have basically "installed" the XCHVSTK.PTI heads on the X350MLD.PTI engine.\par\sect\sectd\sbkpage\headery725\footery743\margtsxn1100\margbsxn940\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\ri445\sl244\slmult1\sb111\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 At\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Main Screen,\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 select\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Make\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Reports\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 option,\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 and\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 pick\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Report\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 Type\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 of\expnd8\ex