\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li1256\ri445\sl244\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Temperature readouts on SuperFlow 60, 110 and 120 benches can be checked by\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 noting that\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the 2 temperatures agree within a couple degrees when the bench has been off for more than 1 hour.\par\sect\sectd\sbkpage\headery725\footery743\margtsxn1100\margbsxn940\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\sl240\slmult1\sb107\f1\fs28\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Weather\expnd-2\expndtw-11  \expnd0\expndtw-2 Corrections:\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li809\ri831\sl244\slmult1\sb237\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Weather significantly affects engine power so it seems natural that one should correct port flow for weather changes. However,\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 engine\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 power\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 depends\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 on\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \f6\b1\i1\expnd0\expndtw0 mass\expnd0\expndtw-1  \f0\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 of\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 air\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 which\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 flows\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 through\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 it,\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 like\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 lbs/minute.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Weather\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 dramatically\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 affects air density, which affects \f6\b1\i1 mass \f0\b0\i0 flow.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Head flow in CFM is a \f6\b1\i1 volume \f0\b0\i0 flow, which does not depend on density.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb4\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li809\ri1110\sl244\slmult1\sb1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Minor weather correction, for factors othe